WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.964
[ROARING]

00:00:01.964 --> 00:00:04.910
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC]

00:00:07.856 --> 00:00:10.311
[CHEERING]

00:00:10.311 --> 00:00:13.257
[PEPPY MUSIC]

00:00:16.210 --> 00:00:17.510
 What's up, everyone?

00:00:17.510 --> 00:00:20.530
This is "Disney+ Deets," where
we break down everything

00:00:20.530 --> 00:00:21.790
you need to know
about your favorite

00:00:21.790 --> 00:00:23.630
Disney+ movies and series.

00:00:23.630 --> 00:00:24.430
I'm Kenneth.

00:00:24.430 --> 00:00:26.740
 And I'm Marcellus, and,
not to do our own horns,

00:00:26.740 --> 00:00:30.250
but we're pretty much the
biggest Disney+ fans out there.

00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:31.300
 No, let's do it.

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:33.110
Toot, toot. 
Beep, beep.

00:00:33.110 --> 00:00:33.910
That's right.

00:00:33.910 --> 00:00:34.780
 Let's get into it.

00:00:38.020 --> 00:00:39.850
KENNETH: I'm assembling a team.

00:00:39.850 --> 00:00:41.160
MARCELLUS: Who are
you, Nick Fury?

00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:42.000
KENNETH: Maybe.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:43.740
I left my eye patch at home.

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:46.680
MARCELLUS: It's time to talk
about Marvel Studios' "The

00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:50.610
Avengers," an epic adventure
full of incredible heroics,

00:00:50.610 --> 00:00:53.610
terrifying villainy, and
mind-blowing special effects.

00:00:53.610 --> 00:00:56.520
KENNETH: It all started with
the Marvel comic created by Stan

00:00:56.520 --> 00:00:59.530
Lee and Jack Kirby in 1963.

00:00:59.530 --> 00:01:03.840
They assembled a team of Earth's
mightiest heroes: the Avengers.

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:06.120
MARCELLUS: In 2012,
that comic book team

00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:08.010
came to life on the big screen.

00:01:08.010 --> 00:01:10.740
This epic installment into
the Marvel Cinematic Universe

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:13.350
completed Phase 1 of
the Infinity Saga.

00:01:13.350 --> 00:01:17.190
It all began in 2008 with the
unforgettable post-credit scene

00:01:17.190 --> 00:01:19.020
in Marvel Studios' "Iron Man."

00:01:19.020 --> 00:01:21.840
 You mean the introduction to
one of my favorite characters,

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:22.800
Nick Fury.

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:24.930
MARCELLUS: You've become a
part of a bigger universe.

00:01:24.930 --> 00:01:26.760
You just don't know it yet.

00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:28.170
KENNETH: That's the one.

00:01:28.170 --> 00:01:30.780
MARCELLUS: According to Kevin
Feige, chief creative officer

00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:33.210
of Marvel Studios, the
idea for "The Avengers"

00:01:33.210 --> 00:01:35.550
actually grew out of
this memorable cameo.

00:01:35.550 --> 00:01:37.410
KENNETH: The easy move would
have been to give the fans

00:01:37.410 --> 00:01:38.970
an Avengers movie right away.

00:01:38.970 --> 00:01:42.480
Instead, Marvel Studios decided
to build out the universe

00:01:42.480 --> 00:01:44.760
one superhero at a time.

00:01:44.760 --> 00:01:46.200
They wanted to
give each character

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:49.050
a chance to shine before
bringing them all together.

00:01:49.050 --> 00:01:51.570
MARCELLUS: The team is made
up of Robert Downey Jr. as Iron

00:01:51.570 --> 00:01:54.990
Man, Chris Evans as Captain
America, Mark Ruffalo

00:01:54.990 --> 00:01:57.540
as the Hulk, Chris
Hemsworth is Thor,

00:01:57.540 --> 00:01:59.490
Scarlett Johansson
as Black Widow,

00:01:59.490 --> 00:02:01.290
and Jeremy Renner as Hawkeye.

00:02:01.290 --> 00:02:03.600
KENNETH: And of course,
Samuel L. Jackson returns

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:06.600
as S.H.I.E.L.D. director, 
Nick Fury.

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:08.280
MARCELLUS: The cast of
heroes for "The Avengers"

00:02:08.280 --> 00:02:11.039
was set from the beginning,
but the filmmakers debated

00:02:11.039 --> 00:02:12.270
who the villain should be.

00:02:12.270 --> 00:02:14.340
In the end, they
decided on Loki,

00:02:14.340 --> 00:02:16.020
partly in tribute
to the very first

00:02:16.020 --> 00:02:17.550
issue of The Avengers comic.

00:02:17.550 --> 00:02:20.070
KENNETH: Like you always
say, Marcellus, every movie

00:02:20.070 --> 00:02:22.010
is only as good
as their villain.

00:02:22.010 --> 00:02:25.280
 Loki, turn off the
Tesseract or I'll destroy it.

00:02:25.280 --> 00:02:26.080
 You can't.

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:28.300
KENNETH: I love Loki,
and Tom Hiddleston

00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:32.410
did such an amazing job bringing
the God of Mischief to life.

00:02:32.410 --> 00:02:34.420
MARCELLUS: The actors all went
through extensive training

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:36.940
with fight choreographer,
Jonathan Eusebio.

00:02:36.940 --> 00:02:39.400
He taught the cast everything,
from medieval fighting

00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:42.760
techniques to Wushu
to kung fu and Kali.

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:44.480
KENNETH: Black Widow is amazing!

00:02:44.480 --> 00:02:46.600
And I love how she
just effortlessly

00:02:46.600 --> 00:02:48.790
is like, OK, let me take
care of this real quick.

00:02:48.790 --> 00:02:49.930
MARCELLUS: [LAUGHS] Right.

00:02:49.930 --> 00:02:52.300
 Just like Budapest
all over again.

00:02:52.300 --> 00:02:54.280
 You and I remember
Budapest very differently.

00:02:54.280 --> 00:02:56.260
KENNETH: To play
Hawkeye, Jeremy Renner

00:02:56.260 --> 00:02:57.820
trained with Olympic archers.

00:02:57.820 --> 00:02:59.410
One of the hardest
tasks to master

00:02:59.410 --> 00:03:01.930
was drawing back his
heavy bow with both speed

00:03:01.930 --> 00:03:03.460
and consistency.

00:03:03.460 --> 00:03:05.920
Hawkeye is the
ultimate master archer,

00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:08.170
so he definitely can't
be slow on the draw.

00:03:08.170 --> 00:03:10.330
MARCELLUS: The rest of the
cast was training hard too.

00:03:10.330 --> 00:03:13.180
Hiddleston and Hemsworth both
did a lot of their own stunts

00:03:13.180 --> 00:03:15.700
to bring a level of
authenticity to the screen.

00:03:15.700 --> 00:03:18.790
Hiddleston knew that the
more you saw an actor's face,

00:03:18.790 --> 00:03:20.683
the more you would be
invested in the characters.

00:03:20.683 --> 00:03:22.150
KENNETH: I liked the
fact that I was getting

00:03:22.150 --> 00:03:24.040
ready to see all of
my favorite characters

00:03:24.040 --> 00:03:24.860
using their superpowers.

00:03:24.860 --> 00:03:25.660
MARCELLUS: Absolutely.

00:03:25.660 --> 00:03:27.400
KENNETH: You had Iron
Man using his suit.

00:03:27.400 --> 00:03:29.380
You had Black Widow
kicking and jumping.

00:03:29.380 --> 00:03:31.060
We had Hawkeye with his bows.

00:03:31.060 --> 00:03:33.970
You had Captain America with his
shield made out of vibranium.

00:03:33.970 --> 00:03:35.680
I was here for it!

00:03:35.680 --> 00:03:36.940
Hulk was smashing!

00:03:36.940 --> 00:03:39.190
Thor was throwing
lightning in his hammer!

00:03:39.190 --> 00:03:41.830
Everywhere I looked
there was action!

00:03:41.830 --> 00:03:44.350
I was on the edge
of my seat, sir!

00:03:44.350 --> 00:03:46.240
MARCELLUS: It was glorious.

00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:48.560
The Hulk got some extra love
from the special effects

00:03:48.560 --> 00:03:49.360
department.

00:03:49.360 --> 00:03:51.850
The goal was to create a
version of the character that

00:03:51.850 --> 00:03:53.200
had never been seen before.

00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:56.590
In previous movies, the
Hulk was entirely CGI.

00:03:56.590 --> 00:03:58.690
For this movie, a
new motion capture

00:03:58.690 --> 00:04:02.450
technology allowed Ruffalo to
play both Banner and the Hulk.

00:04:02.450 --> 00:04:04.610
KENNETH: So when Banner
finally hulks out,

00:04:04.610 --> 00:04:07.870
you realize, whoa, that's
still Ruffalo's face!

00:04:07.870 --> 00:04:10.930
All his expressions have
been captured and transferred

00:04:10.930 --> 00:04:12.940
onto the big, angry, green dude.

00:04:12.940 --> 00:04:14.680
I was here for the Hulk!

00:04:14.680 --> 00:04:16.390
Hulk, smash!

00:04:16.390 --> 00:04:18.670
MARCELLUS: The iconic New York
City moments were actually

00:04:18.670 --> 00:04:20.769
filmed in downtown Cleveland.

00:04:20.769 --> 00:04:23.710
False building facades were
created to transform the city,

00:04:23.710 --> 00:04:26.230
and they even built a
fake New York subway stop.

00:04:26.230 --> 00:04:27.040
KENNETH: Don't worry.

00:04:27.040 --> 00:04:29.200
There's plenty of real
New York in the movie

00:04:29.200 --> 00:04:31.870
too, like the scene shot
at the Bethesda Fountain

00:04:31.870 --> 00:04:32.920
in Central Park.

00:04:32.920 --> 00:04:35.560
MARCELLUS: It takes a lot to
get New Yorkers' attention,

00:04:35.560 --> 00:04:39.100
but Thor walking around Central
Park in his Asgardian cape

00:04:39.100 --> 00:04:40.180
did the trick.

00:04:40.180 --> 00:04:43.540
Huge crowds of paparazzi
and fans showed up.

00:04:43.540 --> 00:04:47.230
 That's how they respond to me
when I'm in my Asgardian cape.

00:04:47.230 --> 00:04:49.210
MARCELLUS: For Feige, it
was important for the story

00:04:49.210 --> 00:04:50.540
to stand on its own.

00:04:50.540 --> 00:04:52.780
He wanted the audience
to enjoy "The Avengers"

00:04:52.780 --> 00:04:54.940
even if they'd never seen
another Marvel movie.

00:04:54.940 --> 00:04:57.280
KENNETH: It's the colorful
personalities of the heroes,

00:04:57.280 --> 00:05:00.040
all banding together
that everyone loves.

00:05:00.040 --> 00:05:03.370
Feige says, it's those
character-driven moments

00:05:03.370 --> 00:05:05.260
that really stick
with audiences,

00:05:05.260 --> 00:05:07.750
even more than the big,
spectacular battles.

00:05:07.750 --> 00:05:09.910
I just love how this
movie gives hope.

00:05:09.910 --> 00:05:12.100
No matter what's going
on, you know the Avengers

00:05:12.100 --> 00:05:13.480
are coming to save the day.

00:05:13.480 --> 00:05:15.280
It just makes you feel good.

00:05:15.280 --> 00:05:18.790
There was excitement seeing
all of my favorite comic book

00:05:18.790 --> 00:05:20.080
characters on screen.

00:05:20.080 --> 00:05:20.980
 You know what, Ken?

00:05:20.980 --> 00:05:25.510
For me, this movie really showed
me that it's all about teamwork

00:05:25.510 --> 00:05:26.410
and coming together.

00:05:26.410 --> 00:05:28.570
Sometimes you disagree,
but if you come together,

00:05:28.570 --> 00:05:31.450
you're stronger than what you
were if you were separated.

00:05:31.450 --> 00:05:33.020
KENNETH: And that's
our show for today.

00:05:33.020 --> 00:05:35.050
Be sure to like,
subscribe, and check

00:05:35.050 --> 00:05:37.780
out Marvel Studios'
"The Avengers,"

00:05:37.780 --> 00:05:39.490
now streaming on Disney+.

00:05:39.490 --> 00:05:41.290
 Take care of yourselves
and the planet,

00:05:41.290 --> 00:05:42.520
and we'll see you next time.

00:05:42.520 --> 00:05:44.320
Marcellus and Ken signing off.

00:05:44.320 --> 00:05:46.240
KENNETH: Marcellus, let's
go join the Avengers.

00:05:46.240 --> 00:05:47.607
MARCELLUS: Ooh, I need
to work out first.

00:05:47.607 --> 00:05:49.540
KENNETH: [LAUGHS] OK.

00:05:49.540 --> 00:05:52.890
[MUSIC PLAYING]

